/** * @file * Installing Custom Modules tutorial template. * * Available
variables: * - tutorial: The tutorial definition. * - images_path: Path to the
tutorial images. */ #} {% set header_content %}
<p>
  The IBM API Connect Developer Portal allows administrators to extend the
  functionality of their site by installing custom modules. These modules can
  either be created internally or downloaded from the Drupal community.
</p>

<p>Before you begin, refer to the official documentation for prerequisites and module compatibility: 
  <a href="https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/SSMNED_12.1.x_cd?topic=extend-installing-custom-modules#tasktapic_portal_custom_module_install_drupal8__prereq__1" target="_blank">Prerequisites for Installing Custom Modules</a>.
</p>

<p>There are two ways to install a module: 
  <ul>
    <li>Complete the <strong>Install from a URL</strong> field.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Choose file</strong> to upload a <code>.tar.gz</code> module file from your local computer.</li>
  </ul>
</p>

<p>In this tutorial, we'll walk through installing a custom module that IBM has created. This module will change the profile page to display the user's <strong>first name</strong> and <strong>last name</strong> instead of the username.</p>
{% endset %} {% set steps_content %} {# Step 1: Clone and Package the Change
Account Display Module #}
<li class="gs-step" data-step="Clone and Package Custom Module">
  <h3>Cloning and Packaging the Change Account Display Module</h3>
  <p>
    Start by cloning the custom module from GitHub. Use the following command:
  </p>
  <div class="command-block">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">git clone https://github.com/ibm-apiconnect/devportal-addons</code></pre>
  </div>

  <p>
    Next, navigate to the module directory and package the module into a .tar.gz
    file:
  </p>
  <div class="command-block">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">cd devportal-addons/apic_v10/modules
tar -czf change_account_display.tar.gz change_account_display/</code></pre>
  </div>

  <p>Now, the module is packaged and ready for installation.</p>
</li>

{# Step 2: Install and Enable the Module #}
<li class="gs-step" data-step="Install and Enable Custom Module">
  <h3>Installing and Enabling the Change Account Display Module</h3>
  <p>1. Log in to your Developer Portal as an administrator.</p>
  <p>2. Navigate to:</p>
  <div class="path-instruction">
    <strong>Extend → Add new module</strong>
  </div>

  <img
    src="{{ images_path }}/navigating-to-add-new-module.png"
    alt="Navigate to Add New Module"
    class="img-responsive"
    loading="lazy"
  />

  <p>
    3. From the <strong>Upload a module or theme archive</strong> section, click
    <strong>Browse file</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    4. Select the packaged module you created earlier (e.g.,
    <code>change_account_display.tgz</code>) and click <strong>Open</strong>.
  </p>

  <img
    src="{{ images_path }}/upload-module.png"
    alt="Upload Module"
    class="img-responsive"
    loading="lazy"
  />

  <p>5. Click <strong>Continue</strong> to install the module.</p>

  <img
    src="{{ images_path }}/installation-successfull.png"
    alt="Installation Successful"
    class="img-responsive"
    loading="lazy"
  />

  <p>
    6. Click the <strong>Enable newly added modules</strong> link to activate
    the module.
  </p>
  <p>
    7. In the filter box, type <strong>Change Account Display</strong>, and
    select the checkbox next to the module name.
  </p>
  <img
  src="{{ images_path }}/checkbox-module.png"
  alt="Enable Module"
  class="img-responsive"
  loading="lazy"
  />
  <p>8. Finally, click <strong>Enable</strong>.</p>

  <div class="success-message">
    <p>The module is now installed and enabled!</p>
  </div>
</li>

{# Step 3: Test Profile Page Change #}
<li class="gs-step" data-step="Test Profile Page Change">
  <h3>Test the Profile Page Change</h3>
  <p>1. Sign out from your admin account.</p>
  <p>2. Log in as a user on your Developer Portal.</p>
  <p>
    3. Click the arrow next to your <strong>username</strong> and select
    <strong>My Account</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    4. You should now see your <strong>first name</strong> and
    <strong>last name</strong> displayed instead of the username.
  </p>

  <img
    src="{{ images_path }}/my-account-page.jpg"
    alt="My Account Page"
    class="img-responsive"
    loading="lazy"
  />

  <div class="success-message">
    <p>
      Congratulations! You've successfully updated the profile page display.
    </p>
  </div>
</li>
{% endset %} {% include 'tutorial-base.html.twig' with { 'tutorial': tutorial,
'images_path': images_path, 'header_content': header_content, 'steps_content':
steps_content } %}
